[{:adr/id "2607125000"
  :adr/title "cloud-itonami-isic-5820/6201 use constant-time bearer-token comparison"
  :adr/status :accepted
  :adr/date "2026-07-12"
  :db/id -1
  :adr/related ["2607124600-cloud-itonami-isic-5820-http-service-layer"]
  :adr/loop-context "Fifth cycle of the /loop dynamic-mode self-paced 'raise maturity toward live production operation' task."
  :adr/decision "Replaced plain (= token presented) with java.security.MessageDigest/isEqual over UTF-8 byte arrays in both cloud-itonami-isic-5820's src/crm/http.clj and cloud-itonami-isic-6201's src/marketing/http.clj, closing the timing-attack gap flagged in ADR-2607124600. No new dependency (JDK standard library). Verified JDK is Temurin 21, length-independent constant-time isEqual behavior confirmed, so no length pre-check was added (that would reintroduce a smaller timing signal). Function contract unchanged."
  :adr/test-status "5820: 50 tests/175 assertions, commit ac1cb62, pushed. 6201: 58 tests/207 assertions, commit f91f8fe, pushed. Both lint clean. New tests are behavioral (wrong-length and same-length-wrong-content tokens correctly rejected), not timing measurements."
  :adr/scope-note "Small, standard security-hardening fix; new ADR only for record-keeping consistency with this fleet's per-change ADR discipline"}]
